Description: scfb: build without the debug tracing.
 scfb_driver.c defines DEBUG to 1 unconditionally, so every server start
 prints the driver's trace on stderr and into Xorg.N.log ("scfb trace: probe
 start", "scfb: PreInit 1", "scfb: ScfbSave 1 done", the mmap addresses, ...).
 It is developer tracing, not log information; the driver's xf86DrvMsg()
 messages are unaffected. DEBUG is set to 0 (the #if DEBUG blocks and the
 TRACE macros compile to nothing).
Origin: NextBSD
 (nextbsd/nextbsd-xlibre#22, item 5)
Forwarded: not yet; X11Libre's and X.Org's scfb both still define DEBUG 1
---
--- a/src/scfb_driver.c
+++ b/src/scfb_driver.c
@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@
 #endif
 
 #undef	DEBUG
-#define	DEBUG	1
+#define	DEBUG	0
 
 #if DEBUG
 # define TRACE_ENTER(str)	ErrorF("scfb: " str " %d\n",pScrn->scrnIndex)
